drm/panel: add the Samsung ANA6706 panel (OnePlus 8 Pro)

The 1440x3168 DSC command-mode panel of the OnePlus 8 Pro
(instantnoodlep / IN2020), exposed at its native 1440x3168 and at the
1080x2376 logical size the phone actually runs Android at.

Shape follows panel-samsung-sofef00.c (OnePlus, Samsung DSC) and this
tree's panel-samsung-ams667xx01.c (patches/0017, Xiaomi alioth), which
was forward-ported to the same 7.2 API this driver targets.

Every number in ana6706_modes[] and ana6706_dsc_cfg comes from the
running phone's device tree (2026-10-25), not from a vendor .dtsi:

  qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-width/height   1080x2376 and 1440x3168
  qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-framerate      60 / 120
  qcom,mdss-dsi-{h,v}-{front,back}-porch, -pulse-width  as tabulated
  qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-width/height   540x72, 720x96, 720x16
  qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-max-level         0x7ff,
  qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-pmic-control-type bl_ctrl_dcs

The vendor DT's four timings are kept in vendor order. timing@1
(1080x2376@120) is the preferred mode: it is the size Android reports
as the logical display and the one gamescope will compose at.

The DCS initialisation sequence is included, transcribed mechanically
from the running phone's device tree (668 bytes, 61 packets, consumed
with no remainder). Its layout and the one difference between the four
vendor timings are documented in the file header.

Not modelled yet, and deliberately so:
 - runtime timing switch (only timing@1 can be driven; ana6706_dsc[]
   is kept for the follow-up)
 - AOD / HBM / MMRM brightness commands
 - Pixelworks Iris initialisation (the pinctrl exposes
   iris_abyp_ready, so a bypass is the expected path)

msm DSI host only supports dsc_slice_per_pkt = 1 while the vendor DT
asks for 2; as on alioth that is tolerated -- the panel's own PPS fixes
slice_width 540 over a 1080 px line, so slice_count stays 2 and the
only difference is one packet per line instead of two.

Signed-off-by: SteamOS for alioth port
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
@@ -1349,3 +1349,13 @@
